 the duplicate_warning seam — omits the two idea() copy sites that already surface duplicate_warning. A grep of the seam being mirrored shows duplicate_warning is re-copied into the idea library return dict (_lib_writes.py:224/231) and re-emitted by the idea CLI (_commands/idea.py:93), neither of which the plan names.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f93e40035dd4a4a90","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, 'Surfacing reuses the advisory seam rather than adding one' and AC line 1 ('library create_ticket return dict, and by MCP create_ticket')","norm_id":"nf0aee59211485a1d","priority":0.3438,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["_lib_writes.py idea(return_alias=True) return dict: similar_tickets is dropped because the dict is built by hand-copying named keys (id, alias, description_warning, duplicate_warning), so a library idea() caller never sees the new advisory.","_commands/idea.py idea CLI: the advisory is never surfaced to stderr for ideas because idea.py re-emits advisories key-by-key via _warn_stderr rather than iterating res."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either add similar_tickets to the idea() return dict (_lib_writes.py:227-232) and _warn_stderr call (idea.py:92-93) alongside duplicate_warning, or make create_core pass through advisory keys generically so new keys propagate without per-site edits; name these sites in the inventory.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State the concurrency model for the shared index: how a reconcile/rebuild write is made atomic (e.g. sqlite transaction or build-to-temp-then-atomic-rename) and idempotent so concurrent creates from CLI/MCP/library cannot tear the file or lose an update, and confirm whether any retire/eviction path is needed or the cache is simply regenerable-on-corruption.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Before serving a query, the index reconciles any tickets whose dir hash has changed since it was last built, then answers. There is no daemon, no background thread'","The plan states three surfaces (CLI, MCP, library) all ride the same create path and the same .rebar/cache index, so two create calls can execute concurrently against one sqlite file","AC covers 'when it is corrupt' only at read/query time, not a writer that produces corruption mid-reconcile; no retire/eviction path is stated"],"finding":"The plan defines the sqlite FTS5 index as shared derived state reconciled synchronously at read-phase before each create, but never addresses concurrent writers: the CLI, MCP server, and library facade can each run `rebar create` against the same `.rebar/cache/similar-tickets/` sqlite file at once, so two processes can both observe a changed dir-hash (check-then-act) and race to rebuild/write the index, and neither a RETIRE/eviction path nor a corruption-recovery-on-write path is specified beyond the read-time 'corrupt index returns empty' case.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa68446b443cdbbf7","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Catch-up is synchronous and read-phase' and 'Persistence'","norm_id":"n9d234bb1fd95cc95","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an Approach note that index reconciliation writes are serialized/atomic (per-process sqlite transaction over a single connection, or write to a temp DB and os.rename), that a corrupt-or-partial index on open triggers a full rebuild (the regenerate-from-tickets-branch retire path), and that concurrent reconcilers converge because the dir-hash is recomputed under the same guard.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define what `score` carries in a `similar_tickets` entry (e.g. raw sqlite FTS5 bm25 value, note it is negative/lower-is-better, or a normalized rank) and document it in 